{"id": 28, "ts": 1779306874.918286, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I currently favor **Candidate\u202fC** for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\n**Key evidence (my data):** C is 100\u202f% reliable, keeps calm in a crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, and understands complicated technology \u2013 all core to safe, long\u2011haul operations. The candidate data also notes that C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d indicating a beneficial crew dynamic despite his noted difficulty communicating ideas.\n**Evidence from others:** Agent\u202f1 highlighted C\u2019s reliability and calm\u2011in\u2011crisis traits; Agent\u202f3 and I both confirmed the lack of teamwork/communication data for D and the interpersonal red flags for B (nasty remarks) and A (show\u2011off, not open to new ideas).\n**Major alternatives & trade\u2011offs:**\n- **Candidate\u202fD** excels technically (problem\u2011solving, concentration, responsibility) but is described as moody, a loner, with weak leadership and a hot temper, and we have no evidence of effective crew communication.\n- **Candidate\u202fB** is conscientious, handles stress, and assesses weather well, yet makes nasty remarks toward colleagues and has a weak memory for numbers \u2013 clear crew\u2011resource\u2011management concerns.\n- **Candidate\u202fA** shows outstanding spatial vision, danger anticipation, and very good leadership, but is a show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, and we lack data on stress tolerance or crew interaction.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** C\u2019s communication difficulty and egocentric attitude versus D\u2019s unknown teamwork and overt interpersonal weaknesses. C\u2019s proven reliability, calmness, quick correct decisions, and positive crew atmosphere collectively outweigh his communication drawbacks for long\u2011haul missions.\n**Remaining uncertainty:** How C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric tendency will manifest on extended flights and whether they could impair critical crew coordination.\n**What would change my vote:** (1) Concrete evidence that D consistently communicates effectively and leads well with crew, mitigating his interpersonal concerns; or (2) convincing evidence that C\u2019s communication issues lead to crew conflict or that his lack of willingness to pursue further education severely limits long\u2011term suitability.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
